    "q-350948": {
      "dom_id": "step-q350948",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}{x}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}={x}^{-2} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int {x}^{-2}\\,dx=-{x}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}{x}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(-{x}^{-1}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}(-{x}^{-1})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})}{{e}^{2}}-(-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)}{1})]+{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}{x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})}{{e}^{2}}+(-{x}^{-1}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{e}^{2}}+(-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}+1) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{3}{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{3}{{e}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
