    "q-350967": {
      "dom_id": "step-q350967",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 1\\cdot \\,dx=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1/2}^{e/2}-{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,(x){|}_{1/2}^{e/2}-{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}x(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{e}{2})\\,(\\frac{e}{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})\\,(\\frac{1}{2})]-{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)-x{|}_{1/2}^{e/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}e-\\frac{1}{2}e+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
